        "title": "Coral Reefs: Biology, Ecology, and Crisis - Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Coral reefs cover less than 0.1% of the ocean floor yet harbor an estimated 25–35% of all described marine species. They are the ocean's tropical rainforests — built by animals, sustained by symbiotic algae, and now being dismantled by a combination of local and global stressors at a rate that outpaces any natural reef-building process."
    },
