      "text": "Hard corals (Scleractinia)     ~830 spp worldwide; ~600 in Indo-Pacific\nSoft corals, gorgonians        ~3,000 spp\nReef fish                      ~4,000 spp  (25% of all marine fish)\nMollusks                       ~5,000+ spp\nCrustaceans                    ~4,000+ spp\nEchinoderms                    ~600+ spp\nSponges                        ~5,000+ spp\nForaminifera                   ~1,000+ spp (key sand-forming organisms)\nMacroalgae                     ~1,000+ spp\nSeagrasses                     ~60 spp (adjacent systems, not reef proper)\nTotal estimate (all taxa)      ~800,000–1,000,000+ spp (most undescribed)\n```"
    },
